course: dictionary
lesson: 8217
title: Reunite: back together again
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To reunite means to bring people together again after they have been apart. The word is built from «re», meaning again, and «unite», meaning join together. «A family at a big parade in New York had not agreed where to meet; their son got separated, and it took police three frightening hours to reunite them.» The family was apart, and the police brought them back together.
explain: Read the second sentence: «A family that agrees a meeting point is reunited much faster than one that does not.» Reunited here means got back together. The clue is the meeting point: a plan helps people find each other again. Try your meaning in the sentence, "A family that agrees a meeting point gets back together much faster than one that does not." It still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: Reunite also means to join parts or groups together again, as when a divided country is joined into one. You will often see it with the word with, as in «be reunited with». The "re" in reunite tells you that the joining happens again.
fact: Reunite means to bring people together again, or come together again, after being apart.
fact: Reunite can also mean to join parts or groups together again, such as a divided country.
fact: The word has two parts: «re» means again, and «unite» means join together.
fact: Common phrases are «be reunited with» and «reunite with», as in «The lost puppy was reunited with its owner.»
fact: Reunite is a verb: reunite, reunites, reunited, reuniting.
exercise: «A family at a big parade in New York had not agreed where to meet; their son got separated, and it took police three frightening hours to reunite them.» What does reunite mean here? | Take a photo of them | Lose them in the crowd | *Bring them back together after being apart | Leave them alone for three hours
exercise: «A family that agrees a meeting point is reunited much faster than one that does not.» Why is that family reunited faster? | Because the parade was small | Because they stopped to rest | Because they walk faster than other families | *Because they agreed where to meet
exercise: «The lost puppy was ___ with its owner at last.» Fill the gap with the right form. | reunites | reunite | reuniting | *reunited
test: The word reunite has two parts: re means again, and unite means join together. What does reunite mean when a country that was split is joined again? | To leave for good | *To join together again | To stop talking | To divide into two
test: Which phrase is correct? Tom hopes to ___ his dog with his family after it ran away. | *reunite with | reunite at | reunite for | reunited from
exam: Which sentence uses reunite correctly? | The boy reunited to the park for lunch. | *The police reunited the lost boy with his mum after three hours. | We reunite our shoes on the bus every morning. | The sky reunited with a loud, sleepy yawn.
